On May 18, 10:10 am, Moonsilence <use...@moonsilence.de> wrote:
> My pet golden naga hatchling called Goldwurm stepped into a level
> teleport trap in the gnomish mines and dissappeared. How far (how many
> levels up or down) can he be? I've searched a lot and am worries that
> I might not find him in time before he goes wild. How many turns does
> this take?
>
> Will a pet that stepped into a polymorph trap stay in his new form for
> ever or just for a number of turns?

1. How far will the pet be?

I think the pet follows the normal level teleport rules: rarely does
it go below the lowest level you've gone, and it can be anywhere from
your current level to DL1.

2. How long until it goes untame?

It depends on how long you've had the pet. Your pet has a tameness
from 0-20 - it goes up one each time the pet eats. So it's likely your
pet had 20 tameness. The tameness value of the pet goes down by one
every 150 turns you are on a different level from that pet. So if you
have had your pet for a while, you have roughly 3000 turns until the
pet becomes un-tame.

3. How long will the polymorph last?

Forever. Unless it turned into a chameleon which itself changes form
often, but that's not likely the case. Your pet will most likely
remain this new form until it's either polymorphed again or dead.

